cartridge "PIRANHAS/JEAN-FRANCOIS SEHAN/1984"

' PIRANHAS - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Jean-Francois Sehan
' ("L'Oric a l'affiche", Editions du P.S.I., 1984). Adapted by Amy & Claude,
' Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this file, ../_common/amy/core.alexis,
' pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): an explorer fell into the Amazon among piranhas.
' The piranhas take turns; on its turn a piranha looks at its four
' neighbours: another piranha there and the two squabble (one is gulped);
' the explorer there and he is caught. Otherwise it swims one cell towards
' him, rows first (up or down to his row, then along it). The explorer is
' much quicker than any one piranha. One piranha left: the river is crossed,
' and the number of moves is shown.
'
' CONTROLS: joystick = swim one cell (held: one cell every 8 frames).
' Title: up/down choose, left/right change the starting level, a button
' confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - River: columns 3-28, rows 3-21 (26 x 19; the Oric's was 30 x 19), the
'   book's '*' frame drawn as muddy banks and reeds, jungle outside.
' - Start positions are fair (the book's could put a piranha next to the
'   explorer, on top of another one, or on the bank): the explorer starts
'   in the middle, no piranha within 5 cells of him, no two piranhas side by
'   side.
' - Three explorers (lives) instead of one game; a catch costs one and the
'   explorer comes back on the safest of 32 random cells, the piranhas stay.
' - Swimming into a piranha is not a catch: the explorer bumps and stays
'   (the book's line 660 lost the game on a mistyped key).
' - A piranha next to both another piranha and the explorer squabbles first
'   (the book checked right, down, left, up in turn).
' - The explorer waves his arms when a piranha is next to him (new: the
'   joystick has no undo).
' - Levels (new): 10 piranhas at level 1, 2 more per level up to 30 (the
'   book: 20-30), and quicker piranhas. Piranha turns: 32 slots in turn, as
'   the book's loop went through all P entries, dead ones included.
' - Score (new): 10 a gulp, a bonus for few moves; the book only showed
'   the moves, which we show too.
' - Colour, animation, music and sound effects are new; the Oric's PING,
'   SHOOT, ZAP and EXPLODE are kept as cues (gulp, fanfare, splash).

